# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. A shell script with CRLF fails on Linux with errors like
#
#     /root/01-provision.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#
# which reads like a broken script rather than a line-ending problem, and has
# cost people hours. `text eol=lf` pins these regardless of the local setting.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else the server executes or parses.
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf

# Let Git decide for everything else.
* text=auto
